<title>JAPAN: Takefuji shares up sharply on share split plans.</title>
<headline>Takefuji shares up sharply on share split plans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Takefuji Co Ltd jumped sharply on Tuesday morning, encouraged by plans for a 1.3-for-1 share split on May 20 and a rise in dividends, traders said.</p>
<p>The share price of the consumer finance firm stood at 8,470 yen as of 0104 GMT, up from its Monday close of 8,320 yen. Volume was 50,000 shares.  </p>
<p>Takefuji said on Monday that it would conduct a 1.3-for-1 share split for shareholders as of March 31, increase its ordinary dividend by 10 yen to 20 yen, and provide a 15 yen commemorative dividend for the year to March 31, 1997.</p>
</text>
